APPENDIX O: Data Notes, Caveats, and Update Protocol

---

O.1 Notes on Data Reliability

1. GDP and Macroeconomic Data: IMF and World Bank figures for 2024–2026 should be treated as estimates and projections subject to revision. Where discrepancies exist between sources, the most recent verified figure is used and the source is cited.
2. Export Data: Automotive export figures vary between MAD- and USD-denominated sources due to exchange rate fluctuations. Where possible, both values are provided. The Office des Changes is the authoritative source for Moroccan trade data.
3. Employment Figures: Employment data for industrial sectors varies between "direct," "indirect," and "total ecosystem" definitions. The appendices specify which definition is used in each case.
4. Local Integration Rate: This politically sensitive metric is reported by industry associations (AMICA, GIMAS) and should be interpreted as an upper-bound estimate. Methodologies for calculation may vary between manufacturers and over time.
5. Patent Data: OMPIC resident patent filings are low in absolute terms. WIPO, USPTO, and EPO data should be consulted for internationally comparable patent output measures. Patent data reflects formal IP protection and may undercount capability embedded in trade secrets and tacit knowledge.
6. NEET and Unemployment: HCP Labor Force Survey data is the authoritative source for Moroccan employment statistics. Figures should be interpreted in the context of Morocco's large informal sector (estimated at 30–40% of employment).

---

O.2 Data Update Protocol

The appendices should be updated annually or as new data releases become available:

· Macroeconomic Data: Update annually (IMF WEO April/October; HCP National Accounts)
· Trade Data: Update quarterly (Office des Changes monthly/quarterly bulletins)
· Innovation Indicators: Update annually (WIPO GII release, typically September; Global Knowledge Index, typically November)
· FDI Data: Update quarterly (Office des Changes; Ministry of Investment)
· Sectoral Data (Automotive, Aerospace): Update annually (AMICA, GIMAS annual reports; Ministry of Industry)

---

O.3 Currency Conversion Note

Unless otherwise specified, MAD/USD conversions are approximated at the prevailing exchange rate for the reference period (approximately MAD 10 = USD 1 for 2024–2025). Precise conversions should be verified against Office des Changes exchange rate data for specific time periods.

